(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Arrays and Hypermatrices", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2cc22455-5a8f-ee47-9f3c-cbd0c62d44db"],

Cell["\<\
WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs` \[LongDash] the objects of the hypermatrix layer\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"7f40010f-2227-9743-b8d1-6154c0644248"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook shows the array object and the hypermatrix built out of them, \
together with the design choices behind them. Everything below is live output \
from src/.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3cd9820-9c7f-6940-b7d4-cd872ca5c90a"],

Cell["\<\
It goes on to the drawing of arrays, the special arrays, the contraction \
operation ArrayMultiply, the entry-by-entry operations that make arrays \
multilinear, and the search for equational identities between array \
operations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8da6aa9d-69ef-484b-8440-f4109400659d"],

Cell["Loading the package", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f1160cab-98d0-5045-9960-54d93f9f9f4c"],

Cell["\<\
The cell below is an initialization cell, which the front end evaluates when \
this notebook is opened. By the time you read this the package is already \
loaded and every symbol is ready to use; the cell is shown for the record, \
and needs no running.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0233cbe-15aa-0249-ae62-b3bd9242ab88"],

Cell["\<\
PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]];
Needs[\"WolframInstitute`Hypergraphs`\"]\
\>", "Input",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"013ce607-83da-0048-bd67-94477316cffb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "PacletInfo.wl in the root of the repository describes the paclet: where its \
kernel sources are, what context they open, and which symbols belong to it. \
PacletDirectoryLoad points the kernel at the repository, and Needs then opens \
the context. Nothing has to be installed, and nothing is copied anywhere \
\[LongDash] the repository itself is what gets loaded, so an edit to src/ is \
picked up the next time the notebook is opened."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"9666af1f-dc5c-494a-8148-6de7204c7173"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Running PacletDirectoryAdd on the same directory, once, would register it \
permanently, and then any of the package's symbols would load it on first use \
in any notebook at all. That writes to the Wolfram user configuration rather \
than to this repository, so it is left as a choice rather than done here."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"433cd1ff-4121-f94c-a7af-100f5af361d8"],

Cell["1. Arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7e849539-2ecd-8849-a4ec-31846a33aa9c"],

Cell["\<\
An array in the Wolfram Language is a nesting of lists. ArrayObject wraps \
such a nesting, and that is all it is: one object for every array, whatever \
its entries are.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"954f0319-326d-514d-879d-6df5c701c447"],

Cell["ArrayObject[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3ce8d28c-ab9b-314c-8e72-187ce7e41d5a"],

