Cell["5. Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d5ac10bd-1893-1748-9c72-212fa473452e"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families of pictures, and an array of any order may be drawn in \
either. The flat family gives plane graphics throughout; the spatial family \
gives cubes arranged in space. Which to use is a matter of what you want to \
see, not of what the array is.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ba18fca4-2c31-ff46-9ffe-564347fa5560"],

Cell["The flat family: ArrayGraphics", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bff3d1fe-2d6e-524e-bfef-9e9b7e49344d"],

Cell["At order one a row of cells, at order two a grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30e5c1ba-740e-3f40-af5d-746eb9139b9b"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"90a91499-535f-2141-a772-4bc7e4cb902a"],

